-- The original DB colocation pg_dump was run with --no-privileges, which
-- stripped every GRANT/REVOKE statement across app+catalog -- not just
-- schema USAGE (fixed separately) but all per-table, per-sequence, and
-- per-function privileges: 1200 grants across 106 tables, gone entirely
-- on yukti-prod. Surfaced by a real Zoho webhook test: PostgREST returned
-- 42501 'permission denied for schema app' even after Exposed Schemas was
-- fixed, because the underlying GRANTs never existed.
--
-- Extracted the exact ACL state from yukti via a fresh --schema-only
-- pg_dump (this time WITHOUT --no-privileges) and applied verbatim to
-- yukti-prod -- not a guessed blanket grant, the real REVOKE-FROM-PUBLIC
-- + per-role-GRANT pattern Postgres/Supabase actually uses, already
-- reflecting every RLS/grant change made earlier this session (e.g. the
-- 8 tables revoked from anon/authenticated stay revoked here too).
-- Verified live: the exact failing REST call now returns 200.

GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA app TO supabase_auth_admin;
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA app TO service_role;
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA app TO authenticated;
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA app TO anon;
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA catalog TO service_role;
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA catalog TO authenticated;
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA catalog TO anon;
